  "term": "idiopathic",
  "definition": "Idiopathic refers to a disease or morbid condition that arises as a primary, distinct disorder rather than as a result, symptom, or secondary effect of another condition or of injury. In historical usage, it often also suggested the characteristic or hereditary form of a disorder.",
